WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.951 --> 00:00:16.293
three days of traveling, Miles and Edward reached Hendon Hall.

2
00:00:16.313 --> 00:00:23.237
"Welcome to Hendon Hall, my king," Miles said as they entered his old home.

3
00:00:23.257 --> 00:00:27.139
"There are seventy rooms and thirty servants here.

4
00:00:27.999 --> 00:00:29.280
Can you imagine that?"

5
00:00:30.844 --> 00:00:34.166
Edward thought of his palace with its hundreds of rooms and servants.

6
00:00:34.186 --> 00:00:36.708
"Actually, I can."

7
00:00:36.728 --> 00:00:42.711
"I've been away for ten years," Miles went on.

8
00:00:42.731 --> 00:00:49.855
"But I'm sure my father, my brother Arthur, and Lady Edith will be overjoyed at my arrival.

9
00:00:51.196 --> 00:00:53.978
Don't be offended if they ignore you in their excitement at seeing me.

10
00:00:55.018 --> 00:00:57.700
They'll soon welcome you into their home and their hearts."

11
00:00:59.832 --> 00:01:01.513
"And what about your other brother?"

12
00:01:02.073 --> 00:01:02.874
Edward asked.

13
00:01:02.894 --> 00:01:07.717
"The one who lied and said you were eloping with Lady Edith?"

14
00:01:09.958 --> 00:01:13.460
"Perhaps Hugh will be polite to us," Miles said quietly.

15
00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:16.042
"That's the best I can hope for."

16
00:01:18.844 --> 00:01:23.467
They entered a spacious room, where a man was writing letters at a table by the fireplace.

17
00:01:23.487 --> 00:01:25.648
"Sit there."

18
00:01:26.632 --> 00:01:29.833
Miles pointed Edward toward a chair and rushed over to the man.

19
00:01:29.853 --> 00:01:33.594
"Hello, Hugh, I'm back!"

20
00:01:34.274 --> 00:01:36.075
Miles said, smiling broadly.

21
00:01:37.635 --> 00:01:39.636
Edward was surprised that this man was Hugh.

22
00:01:39.656 --> 00:01:45.817
"Miles must be so happy to be home that he's even glad to see Hugh," Edward thought.

23
00:01:48.458 --> 00:01:49.919
Hugh shrank back from Miles.

24
00:01:51.159 --> 00:01:54.940
Slowly his stare changed from fear to curiosity to pity.

25
00:01:56.644 --> 00:02:01.586
"From the state of your clothes, poor stranger, the world has treated you harshly," Hugh said.

26
00:02:01.606 --> 00:02:05.888
"I have no idea who you are, and you've obviously mistaken me for someone else."

27
00:02:07.949 --> 00:02:09.629
Miles shook his head in disbelief.

28
00:02:09.649 --> 00:02:14.171
"Are you saying that you don't recognize me, your own brother?

29
00:02:14.811 --> 00:02:15.712
Miles Hendon?"

30
00:02:15.732 --> 00:02:20.014
"Can you really be my lost brother?"

31
00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:23.135
Hugh's face lit up with surprise.

32
00:02:23.155 --> 00:02:25.716
"Let me get a good look at you."

33
00:02:28.244 --> 00:02:29.925
Hugh pulled Miles toward a window.

34
00:02:31.406 --> 00:02:36.188
Then Hugh looked Miles up and down, turned him this way and that, and studied him thoroughly.

35
00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:41.191
Meanwhile Miles laughed and chattered on.

36
00:02:42.632 --> 00:02:44.833
"Yes, it's your dear old Miles.

37
00:02:45.974 --> 00:02:47.495
Oh, this is a great day!

38
00:02:48.515 --> 00:02:49.556
Give me your hand, Hugh!

39
00:02:49.876 --> 00:02:51.077
Let me kiss your cheek!"

40
00:02:52.758 --> 00:02:56.740
Miles was about to hug his brother, but Hugh raised a hand in protest.

41
00:02:57.960 --> 00:02:59.481
"I can't bear this disappointment."

42
00:03:01.283 --> 00:03:03.704
Stunned, Miles couldn't speak for a moment.

43
00:03:05.366 --> 00:03:06.507
"What disappointment?"

44
00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:09.769
Hugh shook his head sadly.

45
00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:16.154
"Perhaps others will notice something that I've missed, but I'm afraid the letter was correct."

46
00:03:17.755 --> 00:03:18.435
"What letter?"

47
00:03:18.455 --> 00:03:24.280
"A few years ago, we received a letter that Miles had died in battle."

48
00:03:25.888 --> 00:03:28.090
"Well, that's obviously not true!"

49
00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:29.711
Miles said angrily.

50
00:03:29.731 --> 00:03:31.652
"Call our father!

51
00:03:32.633 --> 00:03:33.994
He'll recognize me at once."

52
00:03:34.014 --> 00:03:38.056
"I can't summon the dead," Hugh said.

53
00:03:38.076 --> 00:03:40.618
"Our father is dead?

54
00:03:42.039 --> 00:03:44.561
Oh, this is terrible news indeed."

55
00:03:45.001 --> 00:03:47.983
Miles' voice trembled as he struggled to control himself.

56
00:03:48.003 --> 00:03:51.466
"Then let me see our brother, Arthur."

57
00:03:51.486 --> 00:03:54.528
"Arthur has also died."

58
00:03:56.128 --> 00:03:57.089
"Both of them gone!

59
00:03:58.109 --> 00:03:59.530
They were such good people."

60
00:04:01.031 --> 00:04:03.353
Miles stopped to wipe tears from his eyes.

61
00:04:03.373 --> 00:04:08.677
"Please don't tell me that Lady Edith has died too."

62
00:04:10.258 --> 00:04:12.699
"No, she still lives here," Hugh said.

63
00:04:15.181 --> 00:04:16.842
Miles heaved a sigh of relief.

64
00:04:16.862 --> 00:04:21.405
"Then bring her to me—and bring the old servants too."

65
00:04:24.107 --> 00:04:26.321
To Edward's surprise, Hugh nodded.

66
00:04:26.341 --> 00:04:32.526
"Only Margaret and David still work here," Hugh said, "but I'll get them."

67
00:04:35.028 --> 00:04:38.051
After Hugh left the room, Miles went over to Edward.

68
00:04:38.071 --> 00:04:43.015
"It's terrible when no one believes you're the person that you say you are."

69
00:04:43.035 --> 00:04:48.739
"I don't doubt that you are Miles Hendon," Edward said.

70
00:04:48.759 --> 00:04:51.862
"Do you doubt that I'm the king?"

71
00:04:54.256 --> 00:04:57.099
"Uh um Miles was saved from replying by Hugh's return.

72
00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:03.545
The servants were with him, and a beautiful, sad woman walked slowly behind them.

73
00:05:04.866 --> 00:05:08.529
Her eyes were focused on the floor, and she was as pale as a ghost.

74
00:05:10.671 --> 00:05:12.112
Miles sprang toward her.

75
00:05:12.132 --> 00:05:15.315
"Oh, my darling Edith!"

76
00:05:17.377 --> 00:05:20.180
At the sound of Miles' voice, Edith blushed.

77
00:05:22.856 --> 00:05:26.097
Hugh waved Miles away and said to her, "Do you know him?"

78
00:05:27.477 --> 00:05:31.098
Trembling, Edith raised her head and looked into Miles' eyes.

79
00:05:31.118 --> 00:05:34.999
"I've never seen him before."

80
00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:42.121
With a moan and a stifled sob, she fled the room.

81
00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:44.962
"Edith!" Miles cried after her.

82
00:05:47.403 --> 00:05:51.704
Hugh grinned and asked the servants if they recognized Miles, but they shook their heads.

83
00:05:54.292 --> 00:05:58.594
"Well, the servants don't know you," Hugh said after he dismissed them.

84
00:05:58.614 --> 00:06:01.335
"And neither does my wife."

85
00:06:01.355 --> 00:06:03.996
"Your wife!"

86
00:06:05.316 --> 00:06:08.198
In an instant Miles was pinning Hugh to the wall.

87
00:06:08.218 --> 00:06:10.659
"I know what happened!

88
00:06:11.899 --> 00:06:16.901
You wrote that letter yourself, and then you stole the woman I love and everything that's mine."

89
00:06:18.082 --> 00:06:21.603
Hugh wiggled free from Miles' grasp and ran from the room.

90
00:06:22.984 --> 00:06:23.784
Edward jumped up.

91
00:06:24.812 --> 00:06:27.495
"This isn't exactly the welcome you were expecting.

92
00:06:28.356 --> 00:06:29.096
Should we leave?"

93
00:06:30.978 --> 00:06:31.959
Miles scowled.

94
00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:37.685
"Since my father and older brother are dead, I'm the rightful owner of Hendon Hall."

95
00:06:38.786 --> 00:06:40.808
He planted his feet firmly on the floor.

96
00:06:40.828 --> 00:06:44.352
"And I'm not going anywhere!"
